# The Obsidian vault: a separate git repo (maxgttph/learning-vault) checked out
# here so notes and site share one directory. Safe to ignore — Quartz never
# globs vault/, only the symlinks that sync.mjs plants in content/.
/vault/

# Careful: Quartz globs both content/ and quartz/static/ with `gitignore: true`
# (quartz/util/glob.ts), so a rule here does not merely hide files from git —
# it hides them from the build. Adding `content/` silently produced a site with
# zero notes. Anything under those two directories must therefore stay out of
# this file; content/ is excluded from version control via .git/info/exclude
# instead, and the generated assets in quartz/static/fonts and quartz/static/katex
# are committed (regenerate them with `npm run assets`).
